     "content": "```python\nfrom collections import Counter\n\ndef word_count_top(text, k):\n    \"\"\"\n    Counts the frequency of words in a text, cleans them, and returns the k most frequent.\n\n    Args:\n        text (str): The input text.\n        k (int): The number of top words to return.\n\n    Returns:\n        list: A list of (word, count) tuples, sorted by count (desc) and then word (asc).\n    \"\"\"\n    # Lowercase the text\n    text = text.lower()\n\n    # Split on whitespace\n    words = text.split()\n\n    # Define characters to strip\n    punctuation = \".,!?;:\"\n\n    # Clean words: strip punctuation and filter out empty strings\n    cleaned_words = []\n    for word in words:\n        # Strip punctuation from both ends\n        cleaned_word = word.strip(punctuation)\n        if cleaned_word:\n            cleaned_words.append(cleaned_word)\n\n    # Count frequencies\n    word_counts = Counter(cleaned_words)\n\n    # Convert to list of (word, count) tuples\n    items = list(word_counts.items())\n\n    # Sort:\n    # Primary key: count (desc, so use -count)\n    # Secondary key: word (asc)\n    items.sort(key=lambda item: (-item[1], item[0]))\n\n    # Return the top k\n    return items[:k]\n```",
